      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "President Lincoln’s funeral train stopped in San Pierre on May 1, 1875, and a commemorative marker was unveiled there in 2017.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Pierre%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Tierney Park, dedicated in 2017, honors John Tierney, who stowed away on Lincoln’s funeral train from San Pierre to Springfield.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
